2.0.2:

  [Change] tlog wrapper relocated from files/tlog to files/internals/tlog,
        matching LMD's private-tool layout. The /usr/local/sbin/tlog
        user-facing symlink is dropped on all install types (RPM, DEB,
        source). Detection pipeline is unaffected — _rule_tlog() runs
        in-process; the wrapper binary is a dev/debug convenience only.
        Migration note: for interactive byte-offset log debugging, invoke
        /usr/local/bfd/internals/tlog directly or create a user symlink.
        Eliminates per-sync vendored-lib drift (fallback block in the
        wrapper is deleted) and the vestigial TLOG_PATH startup gate.
  [Change] Vendored lib sync: tlog_lib 2.0.5 → 2.0.6, alert_lib 1.0.6 → 1.0.7,
        elog_lib 1.0.5 → 1.0.6, pkg_lib 1.0.9 → 1.0.10, geoip_lib 1.0.6 → 1.0.7.
        All five are comment-discipline cascade bumps from canonical — banner
        separators removed, signature-restatement prose deleted from function
        headers, prose config catalogues replaced with README cross-references.
        Zero functional change in any library; load-bearing rationale (TLS
        posture, symlink-safety, eval-guard validation, pkg_config_merge
        invariants, SIEM/CEF/GELF contract docs, journal filter contracts,
        alert dispatch invariants) preserved intact. Byte-identical to canonical:
        tlog_lib d65158c (v2.0.6), alert_lib 3b66050 (v1.0.7), elog_lib 7a60165
        (v1.0.6), pkg_lib cdd0814 (v1.0.10), geoip_lib cc9559f (v1.0.7).
  [Change] tests/infra: batsman 1.4.1 → 1.4.2 — runs-on input for self-hosted
        runner support (CI workflow only, no test behaviour change).

  [Fix] DEB packaging: /var/log/bfd permissions clobbered by dh_fixperms
        (normalized all directories to 755, overriding the 750 set in
        debian/rules). Postinst now restores 750 at install time, matching
        the existing pattern for /var/lib/bfd/tmp and /var/lib/bfd/stats.
        Pre-existing since DEB packaging was introduced; exposed when the
        DEB install smoke test was run for the first time (never wired
        into CI, only RPM install test was gated).
  [Fix] pkg/test/test-pkg-install.sh: check_link now uses readlink -f
        (canonical absolute path) instead of raw readlink. The old
        comparison only worked for RPM (absolute symlinks); DEB uses
        relative symlinks per dh_link / Debian policy, which caused every
        symlink assertion to fail against the absolute-path expectation.
        Fix works for both package formats.
  [Change] Vendored lib sync: geoip_lib 1.0.5 -> 1.0.6 — restores
           geoip_cc_known() function (regression fix; see canonical
           geoip_lib CHANGELOG for root cause and test coverage).
           BFD does not call geoip_cc_known directly — sync is for
           shared-library discipline (byte-identical vendored copies
           across consumers).

  -- New Features --

[New] CLI subcommand namespaces: bfd ban, bfd ignore, bfd test, bfd cdn,
      bfd report, bfd status — grouped help, bash completion, typo
      suggestions ("Did you mean?"), and bfd help <topic> routing
[New] bfd ignore: add/remove/list/check for ignore.hosts management with
      flock safety, CIDR normalization, and containment checking
[New] bfd status sub-views: lock (PID/age/staleness), cursors (tlog positions),
      pool (attack pool stats), pressure (decay-adjusted scores)
[New] bfd ban history: query across rotated bans.history archives with
      IP filter, time windows (--24h/--7d/--30d), and --json/--csv output
[New] CDN/trusted proxy subsystem: ignore/exclude/derate treatment modes,
      binary-search IP range lookup (IPv4/IPv6), cdn-providers.conf with 5
      default providers, bfd --cdn CLI, CDN_ENABLE and CDN_UPDATE_DAYS config;
      cron.daily auto-refresh and --json output support
[New] Symlink farm enforcement: sbin symlink manifest + runtime self-healing
      (pkg_lib v1.0.6)
[New] Structured audit events for ban escalation, manual ban/unban/flush,
      alert delivery, detection triggers, and scan cycle bookends;
      audit.log added to logrotate
[New] Config validation: REPORT_ENABLED, REPORT_TOP_N, REPORT_CHANNELS checked
      at load time; 8 missing vars added to SIGHUP reload unset block
[New] install.sh creates /usr/local/sbin/tlog symlink for PATH accessibility
[New] Documentation: man page CDN/Trusted Proxy, Country Weighting, and
      SUBCOMMANDS sections; --cdn CLI options, sub-library FILES entries;
      README redesign with SECURITY.md and CONTRIBUTING.md
[New] Color-aware help output: bold section headers respecting NO_COLOR,
      non-terminal, and TERM=dumb
[New] CDN_ENABLE="auto" mode: auto-detect from cdn-providers.conf (uncommented
      entries = enabled); first-run background fetch at install; config_init
      one-shot retry for missing cdn.dat; "0"/"1" still valid overrides
[New] DATA_PATH variable in internals.conf: data files (ipcountry.dat,
      ipcountry6.dat, cdn.dat, cdn6.dat, .last_update) moved from
      $INSTALL_PATH/ root to $INSTALL_PATH/data/ subdirectory

  -- Bug Fixes --

[Fix] RPM/DEB package manifests: add 9 sub-libraries + update-cdn-providers.sh;
      .shellcheckrc and .gitmodules excluded from release tarball
[Fix] File permissions: lock.utime (creation and heartbeat) and ignore.hosts.local
      consistently set to mode 640
[Fix] Report: --7d/--30d correctly maps to weekly/monthly interval; top-IPs
      table emits all 7 columns; messaging templates use JSON-escaped vars
[Fix] --status error for unknown service directed to stderr
[Fix] threat_detected audit event now fires on ban-failed path
[Fix] Multi-channel alert rendering: per-channel dispatch prevents cross-channel
      contamination, Telegram MarkdownV2 escaping for special characters
[Fix] CIDR sidecar enrichment data preserved across all rendering passes
[Fix] pam_generic rule: PREREQ changed from AUTH_LOG_PATH to /etc/pam.d/other
      so journal fallback works on rsyslog-less systems (RHEL 10+, Ubuntu minimal);
      added SYSLOG_FACILITY=10 journal registration (39 of 57 rules now covered)
[Fix] Temp file hardening: extract_hosts uses $INSTALL_PATH/tmp;
      _check_file_safety handles 4-digit setuid/setgid perms
[Fix] show_status "Top services" trailing comma when fewer than 3 services
[Fix] Lock contention message log-file-only when holder is alive
[Fix] Stale IPv6 GeoIP build dirs cleaned up at update-ipcountry.sh startup
[Fix] install.sh: consistent "Updating ... (background)..." format for
      IP country and CDN provider database fetch messages
[Fix] RPM/DEB: exclude.files sed anchored to prevent ignore.hosts.local
      path mismatch (self-ban risk on FHS package installs)
[Fix] RPM/DEB: tlog BASERUN set to /var/lib/bfd/tmp (was /tmp default)
[Fix] RPM/DEB: /var/log/bfd/ created at install time for logrotate
[Fix] RPM/DEB: /usr/local/sbin/tlog symlink for standalone tlog access
[Fix] RPM/DEB: background ipcountry + CDN database downloads on fresh
      package install (matching install.sh pattern)
[Fix] RPM/DEB: cron files marked config(noreplace) to preserve custom
      schedules on package upgrade
[Fix] DEB: explicit daemon-reload in postinst before importconf
[Fix] RPM/DEB: symlink manifest for pkg_fhs_verify_farm() self-healing
[Fix] RPM/DEB: defensive %pre/preinst cleanup for orphaned source-install
      directories (alert/, data/, rules/, tmp/, stats/, internals/, ipcountry.dat)
      to prevent cpio collision when stale dirs remain after partial uninstall
[Fix] FIREWALL validation rewritten as case statement (was for-loop over
      space-split list) — IFS-independent, prevents intermittent CI failures
[Fix] Deep-legacy portability: all bare coreutils (chmod, mkdir, cat, touch,
      ln, cp, mv, rm) use command prefix for CentOS 6 PATH compatibility
[Fix] Unban error message includes hint for firewall-only blocks
[Fix] tlog CLI version mismatch: TLOG_VERSION 2.0.4 → 2.0.5 to match lib
[Fix] status_pressure: use grep -Fq for IP presence check to prevent regex
      interpretation of dot characters in IP addresses
[Fix] tests/43-rules-tier2.bats: jellyfin tests no longer share
      /var/log/jellyfin/log_20260308.log — race under bats --jobs caused
      "auth denied" test to read 3 lines from sibling test's fixture and
      fail with "3 matches" instead of "1 matches". Per-test fixtures now
      live under TEST_TMPDIR; placeholder log in setup_file satisfies the
      rule's existence gate

  -- Changes --

[Change] Vendored lib sync: tlog_lib 2.0.5, alert_lib 1.0.6, elog_lib 1.0.5,
        pkg_lib 1.0.8, geoip_lib 1.0.5
[Fix] pkg_lib 1.0.7 → 1.0.8: POSIX herestring compat, ln -sfn symlink safety
[Change] pressure.conf and pressure-country.conf migrated to whitespace
      format; dual-format parsers for backward compat; importconf auto-converts
[Change] --check shows "no service detected" for rules with log-based PREREQ
[Change] Help output: usage_short() condensed to 22-line three-section layout;
      -h shows full reference, --help opens man page (progressive disclosure)
[Change] conf.bfd reordered: 12→10 sections grouped by admin workflow
      priority; Slack/Telegram/Discord combined into Messaging Alerts;
      Advanced split into Detection Tuning and Logging & Output
[Change] CDN_ENABLE default "0" → "auto" (no behavior change for fresh
      installs — all providers ship commented); runtime guards use _CDN_ACTIVE
[Change] Data file migration: update-ipcountry.sh and update-cdn-providers.sh
      write to $DATA_PATH; importconf migrates from flat layout on upgrade;
      RPM/DEB install to /usr/share/bfd/data/ with legacy compat symlinks
